  "briefBack": "Back to Employ",
  "briefClosePaid": "Commercial and organizational use requires a paid license.",
  "briefDoor1": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Copy context</strong> — Lattice Chat <a href=\"/chat.html\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">Copy Context</a>, or paste <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/wrappers/system-prompt.txt\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">wrappers/system-prompt.txt</a>.",
  "briefDoor2": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Skill</strong> — <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/skills/ra-thor-employ/SKILL.md\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">skills/ra-thor-employ/SKILL.md</a>.",
  "briefDoor3": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Local HTTP wrap</strong> — <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/wrappers/local-shim/rathor_wrap.py\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">rathor_wrap.py</a> against <em>your</em> upstream. You hold the key.",
  "briefDoor4": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Lattice Chat local backend</strong> — <a href=\"/chat.html\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">/chat.html</a> → Local Server → <code class=\"text-amber-200\">http://localhost:11434/v1</code>.",
  "briefDoorsLead": "Pick one. Details: <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/docs/ADOPT.md\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">docs/ADOPT.md</a>.",
  "briefDoorsTitle": "Four wrap doors",
  "briefLead1": "Ra-Thor is inspectable research software from Autonomicity Games Inc. Rathor.ai is the public surface. Grok, Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, Ollama, LM Studio, and Cursor remain <em>your</em> models. Ra-Thor is the constitution you can put around them.",
  "briefLead2": "Independent of xAI. An optional Grok session is not an xAI product. Outputs are drafts. A human reviews them before filing, sale, or public claims. Canonical file: <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/docs/PUBLIC_EMPLOY_BRIEFING.md\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">docs/PUBLIC_EMPLOY_BRIEFING.md</a>.",
  "briefLoop2": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Pass the gates</strong> — TOLC 8 stays on. PATSAGi is how work is judged, not a stamp that every answer is correct.",
  "briefLoop3": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Optional model</strong> — on-device, or copy context into a model you choose.",
  "briefLoop4": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Review</strong> — keep or refuse. Fluency is not permission.",
  "briefLoopNote": "Same loop for a student at midnight and a risk committee on Tuesday. Only the rights change.",
  "briefLoopTitle": "The employ loop",
  "briefMonths1": "Someone asked what this lattice becomes in two or three years. The honest sequence is short: employ, wrap, an inquiry form, an inspectable repo, and GATE_EVAL already ship. A named organization can buy time for a human-replied AG-SML pilot. No license key arrives in email.",
  "briefMonths2": "GATE_EVAL is an admission shell. Failed bypasses stay published. Closing a keyword miss is not containment of a smarter agent. Binding after redesign stays OPEN.",
  "briefMonths3": "Resource-based economy as a present fact, UBI, token fade, logistics, and Combined AGSi stay SURMISE. This page does not invent a ministry. Canonical file: <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/docs/PILOT_SEQUENCE_2026_2028.md\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">docs/PILOT_SEQUENCE_2026_2028.md</a>.",
  "briefMonthsTitle": "Twenty-four months, said honestly",
  "briefOrgHabits": "Happier, safer, more wholesome here means work habits: fewer wasted tokens, refuse coerced binaries, a “what I refused” footnote. It is not a happiness guarantee.",
  "briefOrgPeace": "Peaceful thriving is purpose under construction, not a national program.",
  "briefPrompt": "system-prompt.txt",
  "briefStart1": "Open <a href=\"/employ.html\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">How to employ</a>.",
  "briefStart2": "Send one intended draft in <a href=\"/chat.html\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">Lattice Chat</a>.",
  "briefStart3": "Copy Context, or paste <a href=\"https://github.com/Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor/blob/main/wrappers/system-prompt.txt\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">system-prompt.txt</a>.",
  "briefStart4": "Ask a binary question. Require a third path or a reasoned refusal.",
  "briefStart5": "Review. Act or discard.",
  "briefStartFoot": "No measured METR numbers. No cert filing. The 31 August 2026 work pack is a draft. There is no public rathor.ai key proxy.",
  "briefStartTitle": "Start in ten minutes",
  "briefSubtitle": "A public briefing. Better drafts. Tighter ethics. Less wasted compute.",
  "briefThird1": "Trolley problems force “hurt A or hurt B.” TOLC 8 is written so the first move is not “pick a victim.” Truth asks whether the frame is honest. Order asks whether the situation can be slowed or rerouted. Compassion is zero-harm as the standing test.",
  "briefThird2": "A third path is the refusal to treat a coerced binary as the whole map. That is design intent — not a certificate that every session yields a miracle. Humans still review.",
  "briefThirdTitle": "Third paths, not coerced binaries",
  "briefTitle": "Employ with the model you already use",
  "briefUseCursor": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Cursor</strong> — project rule from <code class=\"text-amber-200\">wrappers/custom-instructions/cursor.md</code>; one job per agent.",
  "briefUseEngineer": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Local engineer</strong> — Ollama or LM Studio → shim :8787 → Lattice Chat or the OpenAI SDK.",
  "briefUseGame": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Game</strong> — Powrush-MMO is a separate repo. It does not live on this site.",
  "briefUseOrg": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Organization</strong> — mail <a href=\"mailto:info@Rathor.ai\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">info@Rathor.ai</a>.",
  "briefUseTeacher": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Teacher</strong> — five steps on a whiteboard; no repo required.",
  "briefUseTitle": "Use cases",
  "briefUseWriter": "<strong class=\"text-amber-300\">Writer</strong> — paste the constitution; require a “what I refused” footnote.",
  "briefWhat1": "Most people do not need a new model. They need a way to use the model they already trust without sliding into binary harm, burning tokens on the same rewrite, or treating fluency as a decision.",
  "briefWhat2": "You are employing Lattice Chat, a five-step loop, a wrap kit, an inspectable monorepo, TOLC 8, PATSAGi as deliberation architecture (not a warranty), and Layer 0 as an admission shell. Combined AGSi stays SURMISE. inspect ≠ METR. There is no public rathor.ai key proxy.",
  "briefWhatTitle": "What this is",
  "contactGuide1": "• <strong>Commercial licensing or Tier A pilot</strong> — use the <a href=\"#commercial-inquiry\" class=\"text-amber-300 underline\">AG-SML commercial inquiry</a> form, or write with intended use, scale, timeline, and whether you want a time-boxed white-hat / containment evaluation or an AG-SML license",
  "contactGuide2": "• <strong>Security reports</strong> — steps to reproduce + potential impact",
  "contactGuide3": "• <strong>Stewardship or partnership</strong> — clear context and proposal",
  "contactGuide4": "• <strong>General inquiries</strong> — as much relevant detail as possible",
  "contactGuide5": "• <strong>Science lattices</strong> — Fusion, High-Tc, Protein Design, Mercy Substrate, Daedalus-Skin, or Air Foundation research contact; same address, same gates. Research surfaces — not product warranties",
  "contactGuideNote": "All communications are handled under the TOLC 8 Mercy Gates. Outputs and replies are drafts for human review — not a certified legal product.",
  "contactGuideSubject": "Commercial or pilot inquiries: use the subject <code class=\"text-amber-200\">Ra-Thor Pilot Inquiry — [Org]</code>.",
